## 3. Design (D-153)
- identity = Supabase Auth access token verified by the server itself (agos_v2/auth.py: JWKS, ES256/RS256 only, alg must match
  the key type, aud=authenticated, iss=<SUPABASE_URL>/auth/v1, role=authenticated, session_id required, exp/leeway).
- every request = one transaction as role `authenticated` with request.jwt.claims set locally (agos_v2/db.py, psycopg 3 pool);
  RLS decides. The service key is never read by the accounts layer; X-API-Key is not a v2 identity.
- 002_accounts.sql: workspace_invitations; roles owner/admin/member; session_is_active() in every policy; forbid_workspace_change
  and stamp_created_by triggers; SECURITY DEFINER functions with fixed search_path; direct writes to workspaces/members/invitations revoked.
- refresh token in an HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Strict cookie scoped to /api/v2/auth; responses no-store; nothing token-like logged.
- 19 routes under /api/v2 (docs/governance/API.md). Unconfigured (no SUPABASE_DB_URL) = 503 on every route.

