## 6. Known Supabase Auth behaviours (measured with the real server, documented in D-153 / SECURITY.md)
- reusing the immediately previous refresh token returns the current active token (GoTrue design, not a bypass);
- reusing an older one after REFRESH_TOKEN_REUSE_INTERVAL -> 401 and the token family is revoked;
- after reuse detection an already-issued access token stays valid until its exp (session row not deleted); explicit logout ends it at once.

